<Layout title="About — Zahin Kabir" active="About"><section class="wrap page-top"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / ZAHIN KABIR</p><h1>Working across<br/>physical systems.</h1><p class="lede">Mechanical design and experimental engineering, informed by an understanding of physical processes.</p></section><section class="wrap prose-grid"><h2>An interdisciplinary<br/>engineering background</h2><div><p>I study Chemical Engineering at Purdue University, with an expected graduation in 2027. My experience spans robotic hardware at Shinkei Systems, R&D and quality engineering at Keurig Dr Pepper, and independent development of an instrumented coffee roaster.</p><p>Chemical Engineering gives me a foundation in heat and mass transfer, experimentation, and manufacturing processes. I bring that perspective to mechanical design: how a machine behaves, what needs to be measured, and how an experiment can guide the next iteration.</p><p>I’m interested in mechanical engineering, robotics, hardware, R&D, mechatronics, automation, and product-development roles.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}experience/`}>Explore my experience ↗</a></div></section></Layout>
